## Example

Here is run through of the major commands to get you going with an Objective-C
project:

### Initialize a project

Choose `executable` and `foundation/objc-developer` at the prompts:

```sh
mkdir myproject
cd myproject
mulle-sde init
```

or

```sh
mulle-sde init -d myproject -m foundation/objc-developer executable
cd myproject
```

### Look at project

``` sh
tree .
mulle-sde files
mulle-sde view
mulle-sde dependency
mulle-sde library
```

### Develop project

Choose the editor of your choice. For a better demo effect, choose one of the
IDEs.

``` sh
mulle-sde edit
```

You don't have to use `mulle-sde edit` though, it's a mere convenience.


#### Add a file

``` sh
mulle-sde add src/MyClass.m
mulle-sde files
mulle-sde ignore src/MyClass.m
mulle-sde ignore src/MyClass.h
mulle-sde files --unmatched-files
mulle-sde reflect
```

#### Craft the project run and debug

``` sh
mulle-sde definition set CFLAGS "-DFOO=1"
mulle-sde check
mulle-sde craft
mulle-sde log
mulle-sde product
mulle-sde run
mulle-sde debug
```

### Look around <project

```
mulle-sde clean tidy
mulle-sde status
mulle-sde craft
mulle-sde status
mulle-sde clean all
mulle-sde status
mulle-sde clean tidy
mulle-sde status
```


### Add a third party dependency

``` sh
mulle-sde add zlib
mulle-sde dependency move zlib top
mulle-sde dependency list
mulle-sde dependency craftinfo set zlib CFLAGS "-DBAR=1"
mulle-sde craft
mulle-sde dependency headers
mulle-sde dependency libraries
```

`mulle-sde clean tidy` and the somewhat less safe `mulle-sde clean gravetidy`
will become important, when doing lots of dependency manipulations.


### Explore dependencies and code

`mulle-sde api` shows the API documentation that ships with your dependencies,
`mulle-sde code` searches and navigates their source:

``` sh
mulle-sde api list
mulle-sde api cat mulle-core
mulle-sde api apropos "how do I allocate memory?"
mulle-sde code grep "mulle_allocator"
mulle-sde code search mulle_malloc
mulle-sde code symbol
```


### Test project

``` sh
mulle-sde test init
mulle-sde test craft
mulle-sde test run
mulle-sde test coverage
```


### Going a little deeper

``` sh
mulle-sde -vv craft
mulle-sde craftorder
mulle-sde craftstatus
mulle-sde environment
mulle-sde patternfile cat
mulle-sde style
mulle-sde tool
mulle-sde howto
```

### Going deep

``` sh
mulle-sde callback
mulle-sde config
mulle-sde donefile
mulle-sde doctor
mulle-sde headerorder
mulle-sde json
mulle-sde link-args
mulle-sde symbol
mulle-sde task list
mulle-sde -ld -ls -lx treestatus
```


